On Tue, Sep 18, 2018 at 05:25:51AM +0000, Oliver Dechant wrote:
> > I don't know about stretchcran.0 archive and there are a couple of
> > versions starting with 2018.  I recommend 20180917 which you can get
> > from unstable.  I released it *especially* for you since you obviously
> > had not set DEBFULLNAME and DEBEMAIL. (Did you fixed now?)
> I've made the updates locally. Thank you for the revisions to dh-r, the
> scripts are very interesting. I don't think stretchcran0 is actually an
> archive, I have a Debian Science Team maintained project under --
> Filename: stretch-cran35/dh-r_20180403~stretchcran.0_all.deb.

The Maintainer name is probably not relevant.  Those Debian packages are
consumed by lots of derivatives.  The name seems to be a sign that you
somehow have

    http://cran.wustl.edu/bin/linux/debian/stretch-cran35/

in your sources.list.  For the purpose of Debian package development it
is dangerous to consume third party apt sources since it could lead to
wrong assumptions what package exists and what not.

> > It seems we keep on misunderstanding.  We are talking about packages
> > inside the Debian archive and there is no gmp package.  If
> > prepare_missing_cran_package you can be pretty sure that it is needed
> > for your target package (and you need to add this to Build-Depends
> > manually later).  Can you please confirm that you understood what
> > pbuilder is and that you are using it?
> I know of pbuilder from the maintainers guide. I can follow the
> maintainers guide.

Yes, that would be helpful.

